data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Tokenize each document with the regular expression `(?u)\\b\\w\\w+\\b` after lowercasing. Count the tokens\nper document. Count, for each term, how many documents contain it. The idf of a term is\n`ln((1 + n) / (1 + df)) + 1`. The weight is the count times the idf. Divide each row by its l2 norm, and\nleave a row of zeros as zeros."},"hints_note":null}

